# Replaces a generic Python-project template that had been sitting here
# since this repo's initial scaffolding despite this being a pure
# Next.js/TypeScript app — found to be actively harmful, not just
# irrelevant: its bare `lib/` rule (meant for a Python package build
# directory) matched this app's own src/lib/ too, silently hiding every
# file added there from `git add` with no error. Confirmed via
# `git ls-files` that the one pre-existing file under src/lib/
# (events.ts) had been committed before this mattered and was
# unaffected; the new files added alongside the BEAU/ORBI/VELA shared
# auth work (src/lib/entitlements.ts, src/lib/supabase/*) were the ones
# actually caught silently ignored, here.

# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Next.js build output
.next/
out/

# Env files with real secrets — only .env.example is ever committed
.env*.local
.env

# Vercel
.vercel

# Misc
.DS_Store
*.pem
npm-debug.log*

# TypeScript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Playwright
/test-results/
/playwright-report/
/blob-report/
/playwright/.cache/
